<code>assert index >= 0 && index < this.size() => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)));</code>

This assert statement ensures that if the index is within the valid range of the list, then for every index `i` less than the specified index, the element at `i` remains unchanged or continues to be `null` after the operation.
